# CreditLens — example environment configuration
#
# CreditLens runs entirely on locally generated SYNTHETIC data and requires NO
# external API keys or secrets. The only configurable values are the host/port
# for the FastAPI service and the frontend dev port. Copy this file to `.env`
# and adjust if the defaults conflict with something on your machine.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# ---- Backend (FastAPI / uvicorn) ----
# The API host/port are NOT read from environment variables — set them on the
# uvicorn command instead (local: `uvicorn creditlens.api.app:app --host
# 0.0.0.0 --port 8002`). In a container the Dockerfile CMD binds
# `--host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8002}`, honoring an injected $PORT
# (Render / Cloud Run set this automatically).

# ---- Frontend (Next.js) ----
# Base URL of the live CreditLens engine. The web demo calls POST /score and
# POST /explain against this URL and renders the REAL logistic scorer + SHAP output.
# If the backend is unreachable the UI automatically falls back to its
# in-browser demo model (no crash, build still works). Must be set at BUILD
# time for production (`next build`) because NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8002

# Note: `uvicorn creditlens.api.app:app --port 8002` and `npm run dev` (port
# 3003) work out of the box without any .env file. For the full stack in one
# command, use `make demo` (Docker) or `make demo-local` (no Docker).
